    20	 *   phases itself (local resolution, then a write, then a refresh).
    21	 * - {@see self::runOperation()} — a single atomic operation (typically one
    22	 *   gateway call) whose documented phases all settle together from the
    23	 *   outcome. Every phase row animates while the work runs, then all rows settle
    24	 *   green on success. On failure no row is falsely marked done — only the
    25	 *   footer turns red. Use for atomic gateway mutations so the tree never claims
    26	 *   a phase completed when the call ultimately failed.
    27	 *
    28	 * Animation while a blocking closure runs is driven by a forked ticker process
    29	 * that repaints the active rows every frame interval. When the output is not
    30	 * decorated (tests, piped output) no process is forked and only settled rows
